   "date": "2018-09-23T16:59:45Z",
   "subject": "Re: MIRT - Help with longitudinal measurements",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">At this stage of your theory, I would probably recommend not using IRT due to its computational complexity. You might want to try a SEM (e..g, via lavaan) approach first to determine what approximately works well, and make decisions from there. It&#39;s possible to go about these analyses using IRT, but the estimation times will be noticeably large and likely less flexible than more developed alternatives. HTH. <div><br clear=\"all\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_signature\" data-smartmail=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Phil</div></div></div></div><br></div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\">On Tue, Sep 18, 2018 at 10:03 PM Hugo Harada &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">hugo....@adaptativa.com.br</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
